<figure class="gateway-attachment-map" aria-labelledby="gateway-attachment-title">
  <figcaption id="gateway-attachment-title"><span class="content-kicker">Two independent handshakes</span><strong>Attaching a Route and referencing its backend cross different trust boundaries.</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="attachment-columns">
    <section>
      <header><small>Infrastructure namespace</small><b>Gateway listener</b></header>
      <div class="rules"><span>allowedRoutes</span><span>Route kind</span><span>Hostname</span></div>
      <i aria-hidden="true">accepts? ↔ requests?</i>
      <header><small>Application namespace</small><b>HTTPRoute parentRefs</b></header>
      <footer><strong>Attached</strong><span>Both sides and hostname intersection agree</span></footer>
    </section>
    <section class="backend-trust">
      <header><small>Application namespace A</small><b>HTTPRoute backendRef</b></header>
      <div class="rules"><span>Group</span><span>Kind</span><span>Name + port</span></div>
      <i aria-hidden="true">references? ↔ grants?</i>
      <header><small>Backend namespace B</small><b>ReferenceGrant</b></header>
      <footer><strong>ResolvedRefs</strong><span>Backend owner explicitly permits the reference</span></footer>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p><b>One does not imply the other.</b> `allowedRoutes` governs attachment to the listener; `ReferenceGrant` governs a supported cross-namespace object reference.</p>
</figure>

